## Notes on Arguments and Attributes

- `policy_type`: Changing this forces a new resource.
- `allow_override`: Defaults to `false`.
- `id`: ID of the policy.

## Import

Policies can be imported using their numeric ID:

```shell
terraform import portainer_policy.example 42
```

Portainer does not return the configured `environment_type`, only the environment types the policy type applies
to. The import sets `environment_type` when that is a single type (the Kubernetes policy types); for the Docker
policy types (`docker`, `podman`, `swarm`) it stays unset, and the next plan sets it from the configuration
(an in-place update).
